    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds too vague and corporate. if a reporter asks a direct question like \"why did the candidate vote against this funding?\" a meeting with a \"small committee\" isn't going to stop the bleeding. they're going to point at the vote record and say they backstabbed the community. \n\nwe need a specific narrative. is there any way we can frame the actual vote so it doesn't look like they were just being against the center itself? maybe there was something wrong with the bill or the way it was structured?",
