      "content": "that's a solid angle, but we gotta be careful. if a hard-hitting reporter asks for the specific \"exclusionary measures\" we're talking about, we might run into trouble because the actual text of the bill doesn't really support that. the bill was pretty straightforward. \n\nif they call our bluff and ask for proof that the bill was \"riddled with flaws,\" what's our fallback? can we just stay on the \"equity\" talking point, or do we need to be more specific about what was actually wrong with the document so we don't look like we're lying?",
